  "summary_en": "Journal article arguing that violations of robots.txt by web crawlers, especially generative-AI scrapers, can ground civil liability in common law jurisdictions through unilateral contract and tort (trespass to chattels, negligence). Includes an empirical survey of top websites' robots.txt files. Concerns software web robots, not physical robots.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Robots.txt can operate as a unilateral contract offer accepted by conduct when a bot accesses the site.",
   "Robots.txt can serve as notice establishing tortious liability, including trespass to chattels and negligence.",
   "Civil doctrines are more balanced than criminal or copyright remedies for regulating web scraping.",
   "Empirical analysis of top 200 websites shows growing robots.txt blocking of LLM-training crawlers.",
   "Clarifying liability helps counter internet fragmentation and preserve openness."
  ],
